## Exact localization and evidence limits

The fixed diagnostic fields are:

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| captured_check | module_origins_check_12 |
| captured_function | module_origins |
| exception_class | ProbeError |
| probe_error_code | distribution_rejected |
| module_family | transformers |
| phase | inputs |
| origin_category | source |

The hash-frozen observer's lines 322–323 compare the direct module dictionary:
`str(vars(sys.modules[name]).get("__version__")) == _STATE["versions"][name]`.
The current name was `transformers`; its lock requires `5.15.1`. This equality
returned false. Torch's preceding equality and the preceding complete scanned
module-root/core checks had passed in this observed witness.

**Do not interpret `origin_category=source` as Transformers loading from source.**
The diagnostic's context reader saw the lingering `resolved` local from the
previous module scan while `name` had advanced to the separate version loop.
The field is stale context for this particular predicate, not a path-origin
failure. The report contains no actual version value, field-presence flag or
type, so it cannot distinguish an absent direct-dictionary value, lazy attribute
exposure, an unusual value, or a genuine version mismatch. A lazy-module issue
is only a hypothesis. No OverlayFS, inode or native-mapping cause is established.

`distribution_versions()` and `native_origins()` follow `module_origins()` in
the witness; this failed witness did not complete those checks. Aggregate
retained telemetry: 55,418 observed need checks; 1 witness started, 0 completed;
2 failure messages, 1 retained deduplicated packet; 0 completed invocations,
rank workers or origin observations. These are bounded observations, not proof
of all unseen child work. Frozen stage/code: worker `inputs/synchronize_failed`,
probe `worker_run`, fixture `ledger`, child `run`.

